  "extractionNotes": "Grant evidenced only by the file label (right granted); no ZUS decision, note or screen in the file, so every period and rate is the claim or inferred. Full-time employment 2013-08-01..2023-12-31, terminated by notice because the workplace was liquidated (work certificate dated 2024-01-02; shortened notice not applied). ZAS-55 dated 2024-01-02 with the statement that no other employment was offered; its start date is redacted, so the Art. 30 block is inferred from the day after termination to the day before the birth. Doctor's certificate for ZUS dated 2023-12-21 states a first-trimester pregnancy, i.e. pregnancy during employment. Z-3 salary table 2023-01..2023-12 at the minimum wage of each half-year (3490.00, then 3600.00), all days worked; payer up to 20 insured. ZAM (undated) asks for maternity 2024-07-24..2024-12-10 and parental 2024-12-11..2025-07-22 with the full-length declaration ticked. The birth extract carries a handwritten date of 2024-07-29, which conflicts with the ZAM; a former employee cannot start maternity before the birth and the Art. 30 benefit runs to the birth, so the birth date is inferred from the ZAM start (2024-07-24). asOf is set to the inferred birth date (the ZAM is undated) and adjudication mode is explicit. Rates not in file: 100% for the Art. 30 benefit and 81.5% for maternity + parental expected."
